Parity disposition: the web <RangePicker> takes `value` as a prop and `onChange` as a callback; its only
hook is `useTranslation`. The native peer keeps that contract — the page's current range + props arrive via
the P1/S8 RangePickerSource snapshot and commits route back out through the page-supplied onChange /
onCompareChange closures (the host owns the URL/query state, exactly as the web page does). Every REAL web
branch is reproduced: the trigger (active-preset label + formatted range), the preset listbox (immediate
commit + close, "all" floored by resolveAllTimeStart(minDate)), the 2-month range calendar (stage-only;
Apply commits; Cancel/dismiss discards; Apply disabled until dirty), the compare toggle vs the staged
"{{count}} days" summary, and the presetsOnly variant (calendar+footer hidden). The prompt's leaf-state
template (loading / empty / error / stale / offline) is reproduced via the source seam — bound to the REAL
async dimension of the picker's resolvable range/bounds (the web `minDate` = "user's first data point"),
never fabricated chrome. Charts/maps: NONE in source → NONE here.

